Azure DevOps Engineer – Interview Questions (4–6 Years Experience)

If you’re preparing for an Azure DevOps Engineer role, these are the real interview questions you should be comfortable answering 👇

🔹 Azure Architecture & Design
How do you design a highly available application on Azure?
When would you choose Azure Load Balancer vs Application Gateway?
How do you design multi-region deployments in Azure?
How do you implement zero-downtime deployments in Azure?
How do you plan disaster recovery and backups in Azure?

🔹 CI/CD with Azure DevOps
How do you design CI/CD pipelines using Azure DevOps?
YAML pipelines vs Classic pipelines — when do you prefer each?
How do you handle approvals and gates in Azure DevOps?
How do you implement rollback strategies in Azure deployments?
How do you secure Azure DevOps pipelines?

🔹 Containers & Kubernetes (AKS)
AKS vs ACI vs App Service — when would you use each?
How do you deploy and scale applications on AKS?
How do you troubleshoot pod failures in AKS?
How do you handle AKS upgrades with minimal downtime?
How do you secure workloads running on AKS?

🔹 Infrastructure as Code
Terraform vs ARM vs Bicep — what do you choose and why?
How do you manage Terraform state securely in Azure?
How do you prevent configuration drift in Azure infrastructure?
How do you design reusable IaC modules?
How do you manage secrets in IaC?

🔹 Monitoring, Logging & Reliability
Which Azure Monitor and Log Analytics metrics matter most?
How do you design alerts without alert fatigue?
How do you centralize logs across subscriptions?
How do you reduce MTTR during Azure incidents?
How do you implement SLIs and SLOs in Azure?

🔹 Security & Cost Management
How do you implement least-privilege access using Azure AD?
How do you secure Azure Storage, VMs, and SQL databases?
How do you manage secrets using Azure Key Vault?
How do you optimize Azure costs in production?
How do you handle security incidents in Azure?

💡 Azure DevOps interviews focus on design decisions, automation, and reliability — not just services.
